<!--
  Name:     SNECMA_M53-P2
  File:     SNECMA_M53-P2.xml
  Author:   Richard Harrison (rjh@zaretto.com)
  Date:     20 September 2017

  SNECMA M53-P2 afterburning low-bypass turbofan. Powers the Mirage 2000
  (single engine).
    * Single-shaft, bypass turbofan engine
    * 3-stage LP compressor
    * 5-stage HP compressor
    * Annular combustion chamber
    * 2-stage cooled turbine
    * Annular A/B chamber
    * Variable-section convergent flap-type nozzle
    * Full authority digital engine control (FADEC)

  Published specifications (M53-P2):
    Military (intermediate) thrust:  14,500 lbf (64.3 kN)
    Maximum (afterburning) thrust:   21,400 lbf (95.1 kN)
    Bypass ratio:                    0.36:1
    TSFC (military):                 0.88 lb/(lbf.h)
    TSFC (max afterburner):          2.06 lb/(lbf.h)
    Mirage 2000 max speed:           ~Mach 2.2 (airframe/inlet limited)

  Modelling approach
  ==================
  JSBSim FGTurbine thrust formulas (from FGTurbine.cpp):
    Idle:        thrust_idle = milthrust * IdleTable(mach, alt)
    Military:    thrust = thrust_idle + (milthrust - thrust_idle) * MilTable(mach, alt)
    Afterburner: thrust = maxthrust * AugTable(mach, alt)

  Note the asymmetry: military thrust is CUMULATIVE on idle (so it can never
  fall below idle), but afterburner thrust is maxthrust * AugTable directly.
  This is why all three tables are normalised so that the Mach 0 / sea-level
  entry = 1.0 (giving rated static thrust with the scalars above) and why the
  table ceilings are aligned (all terminate at 75,459 ft = 0) - otherwise AB
  thrust could fall below idle near the top of the tables.

  The Mil/Aug table SHAPES are a NET installed-thrust model (gross corrected
  thrust MINUS ram drag), fit to the USSR-MoD-1984 reference points. An earlier
  version modelled only the gross side (thrust ~ ram total-pressure ratio Pt2)
  and omitted ram drag; that made low-altitude thrust rise far too steeply with
  Mach (SL M0.8 AB came out ~+55% over the reference, which actually shows a
  slight transonic DROP). Net thrust = gross - ram drag, and ram drag is large
  near the ground (dense air) and small at altitude, so the omission only hurt
  low/mid altitude. The corrected shape (autotest/references/gen-thrust-tables.py):

    Fhat(M,h) = L(h) * G(M) * R(M,h)            (normalised, =1 at M0/SL)
      L(h) = delta(h)^n         static altitude lapse (n: mil 0.63, AB 0.69)
      G(M) = (1+0.2 M^2)^3 * eta_inlet(M)        gross corrected-airflow rise
      R(M,h)= 1 - beta * M*sqrt(theta)/sqrt(1+0.2 M^2)   ram-drag momentum loss
      eta_inlet = 1 (M<=1); 1 - 0.075*(M-1)^1.35 for M>1   (MIL-E-5008R)
      beta = a_SL / Vjet : mil 0.503, AB 0.470 (AB keeps more thrust with Mach
             because its jet velocity is higher -> AB/Mil ratio rises with Mach)

  This reproduces the classic transonic thrust "bucket": at SL, AB dips to
  ~0.90 (M0.4) and 0.93 (M0.8) before rising supersonically; mil dips to ~0.87.
  Anchor fit: AB within 0.9%, mil within 3% of the reference at SL/5.5km/11km
  M0.8. Mirage 2000 is airframe-limited to ~M2.2; the M2.5 row and the columns
  above ~50k ft are physical extrapolation, not anchored to data. The IdleThrust
  table is unchanged (idle is a few % of thrust; its Mach shape is immaterial).

  THRUST RATING / DEC: FGTurbine itself does not model FADEC flat-rating or
  TIT-limited derating against true ambient temperature. To approximate it,
  the thrust tables are indexed on propulsion/engine[0]/dec/rating-altitude-ft
  (computed in Systems/Mirage-2000-engines-Snecma-M53.xml) instead of raw
  atmosphere/density-altitude:
      rating-altitude = max(pressure-altitude, density-altitude - corner)
  This keeps the hot-day derate that density-altitude already provided while
  adding the cold-day flat-rate cap (no spurious over-thrust), and on an ISA
  day reduces exactly to density-altitude so this calibration is unchanged.

  History
  =======
  2017-09-20  RJH  Initial version (thrust shape derived from F110/NASA tables)
  2026-06-05  RJH  Rebuilt thrust tables on the F100-PW-220 corrected-thrust
                   model (shared normalised shape, M53 scalars):
                   - AugThrust given its own distinct shape (was identical to
                     MilThrust, pinning AB/Mil ratio at a constant ~1.48)
                   - Aligned table ceilings at 75,459 ft (fixes AB < idle
                     artifact at 80,000 ft reported by Josh)
                   - Normalised so M0/SL produces rated static thrust
  2026-06-08  RJH  Rebuilt Mil/Aug tables on a NET installed-thrust model
                   (gross MINUS ram drag), fit to the USSR-1984 anchors. The
                   2026-06-05 gross-only shape over-rammed at low altitude
                   (SL M0.8 AB +55% vs reference); the net model restores the
                   transonic thrust bucket. Generator: autotest/references/
                   gen-thrust-tables.py. DEC rating-altitude column indexing unchanged.
  2026-06-08  RJH  Built Mach+altitude SFC tables (USSR-1984 Fig 2.4 dry /
                   Fig 2.2 AB) to fix the missing-Mach-term SFC error (~30% low
                   at M0.8). BUT stock FlightGear's FGTurbine reads tsfc/atsfc as
                   a SCALAR only, so the tables are kept COMMENTED OUT next to the
                   shipping scalars (0.88 / 2.06) and activated once FG ships a
                   JSBSim with FGFunction-tsfc support (~2026). See SFC section
                   above. Tables validated on the aceFM JSBSim: SFC 1.05 (11km
                   M0.8) / 1.15 (SL M0.8) within 2% of the figures.

  References
  ==========
  [1] JSBSim FGTurbine.cpp thrust calculation source code
      https://github.com/JSBSim-Team/jsbsim/blob/master/src/models/propulsion/FGTurbine.cpp
  [2] Companion model F-15/Engines/F100-PW-220.xml (corrected-thrust derivation)
  [3] Safran M53 fact sheet
      https://web.archive.org/web/20171026223525/https://www.safran-aircraft-engines.com/file/download/fiche_m53_ang_2011.pdf
-->

<turbine_engine name="SNECMA_M53-P2">
    <milthrust>     14500 </milthrust>
    <maxthrust>     21400 </maxthrust>
    <bypassratio>    0.36 </bypassratio>
    <!-- ================================================================
         SFC (tsfc / atsfc) - SHIPPING: scalar.  See the SFC section in the
         header block for the full rationale.

         Stock FlightGear's FGTurbine (FGTurbine.cpp, D. Culp) reads tsfc/atsfc
         with FindElementValueAsNumber - i.e. a SINGLE NUMBER - and hardwires
            correctedTSFC = tsfc * sqrt(T/389.7) * (0.84 + (1-N2norm)^2)
         inline (no Mach term). A function/table here would parse as 0 and the
         engine would burn NO fuel. So a scalar is the only form stock FG accepts.

         CONSEQUENCE: installed SFC is Mach-independent and reads ~30% low at
         M0.8 vs the USSR-1984 figures. This cannot be corrected via config on
         stock FG; it needs the FGFunction-tsfc support in the newer JSBSim
         (aceFM build, expected in FlightGear ~2026).

         WHEN THAT SHIPS: delete the two scalars immediately below and uncomment
         the "FUTURE" table block beneath them (kept here so the calibrated work
         - validated to within 2% of Fig 2.4/2.2 - is not lost).
         ================================================================ -->
    <tsfc>            0.88 </tsfc>
    <atsfc>           2.06 </atsfc>

    <!-- FUTURE Mach + pressure-altitude SFC TABLES (requires FGFunction <tsfc>
         support; will NOT work on stock FG - see note above). Digitised from
         USSR-1984 Fig 2.4 (max dry) and Fig 2.2 (full AB), kg/(kgf.h)==lb/(lbf.h).
         Indexed on actual pressure-altitude (NOT the DEC thrust rating-altitude):
         fuel flow follows real conditions, not the flat-rating cap. The dry table
         is x a part-throttle penalty (0.84+(1-thr)^2)/0.84 (=1 at military, rising
         below it - the part-power term FGSimplifiedTSFC had). Validated 2026-06-08:
         SFC 1.05 (11km M0.8) and 1.15 (SL M0.8) within 2% of the figures.
         TO ACTIVATE: delete the two scalars above and uncomment this block.

    <tsfc>
      <product>
        <table>
          <independentVar lookup="row">velocities/mach</independentVar>
          <independentVar lookup="column">atmosphere/pressure-altitude</independentVar>
          <tableData>
                        0      18044      36089      60000
            0.0     0.900      0.900      0.910      0.910
            0.2     0.920      0.920      0.930      0.930
            0.5     1.020      0.980      0.950      0.950
            0.8     1.150      1.100      1.050      1.050
            1.0     1.300      1.200      1.120      1.120
            1.2     1.450      1.300      1.200      1.200
            1.5     1.580      1.420      1.300      1.300
            2.0     1.750      1.580      1.500      1.500
            2.5     1.900      1.720      1.650      1.650
          </tableData>
        </table>
        <quotient>
          <sum>
            <value>0.84</value>
            <pow>
              <difference>
                <value>1.0</value>
                <max><value>0</value><min><value>1</value><property>fcs/throttle-pos-norm[0]</property></min></max>
              </difference>
              <value>2</value>
            </pow>
          </sum>
          <value>0.84</value>
        </quotient>
      </product>
    </tsfc>
    <atsfc>
      <table>
        <independentVar lookup="row">velocities/mach</independentVar>
        <independentVar lookup="column">atmosphere/pressure-altitude</independentVar>
        <tableData>
                      0      18044      36089      60000
          0.0     2.050      2.050      2.050      2.050
          0.2     2.100      2.100      2.100      2.100
          0.5     2.300      2.250      2.050      2.050
          0.8     2.550      2.350      2.100      2.100
          1.0     2.650      2.420      2.150      2.150
          1.5     2.750      2.450      2.200      2.200
          2.0     2.850      2.550      2.250      2.250
          2.5     2.950      2.650      2.350      2.350
        </tableData>
      </table>
    </atsfc>
    -->
    <idlen1>         47.0 </idlen1> <!-- We think N1 and N2 are the same due to single spool engine -->
    <idlen2>         47.0 </idlen2>
    <maxn1>         102.0 </maxn1>
    <maxn2>         102.0 </maxn2>
    <augmented>         1 </augmented>
    <augmethod>         2 </augmethod>
    <!-- acceleration from 0 -> 15% (at which point the start logic takes over in FGTurbine using 1.2 and 2.0 for N1/N2 acceleration rate) -->
    <n1spinup>          1 </n1spinup>
    <n2spinup>          3 </n2spinup>
    <injected>          0 </injected>
    <ignitionn1>        0 </ignitionn1> <!-- There is no such thing as clicking on the cut during startup (it's done before) -->

    <n1startrate>      0.85</n1startrate> <!-- start spool-up rate; tuned for a ~30 s start -->
    <n2startrate>      0.85</n2startrate>

    <!--
        IdleThrust: fraction of milthrust produced at idle power setting.
        Scales with ram effect (Mach) and air density (altitude).
    -->
    <function name="IdleThrust">
